\description{
Each source has different patient ID columns (e.g. stay_id vs
patientunitstayid). This function UNION ALLs harmonized source outputs into a
single target schema (default: "rendehr"). For time series,
\code{analysis_level = "admission"} reads the native-grain \code{ts_tab}, and
\code{analysis_level = "icu"} reads the derived ICU projection \code{ts_icu} created by
\code{make_icu_timeline()}. In the merged time-series table, \code{src_icu_id} is always
the native/source ICU ID. The projection columns \code{assigned_icu_id},
\code{event_origin}, and \code{icu_time_relation} are emitted only for
\code{analysis_level = "icu"} (omitted in admission mode, where they would be all
NULL). The merged \code{ehr_id} is grain-specific: \code{analysis_level = "admission"}
keys on \code{src_patient_id + src_admission_id}, while \code{analysis_level = "icu"}
additionally appends the (assigned) ICU id. It is recomputed from the source
